From: surface-kit
Subject: [PATCH] media: intel: ipu4: don't follow a link csi2 debug taps don't have

The CSI-2 debug capture nodes are left out of the media graph unless
debug_capture_links=1, but ipu_isys_video_init() still calls their
try_fmt_vid_mplane (csi2_try_fmt) to pick a default format. csi2_try_fmt
takes list_first_entry() of the node's links unconditionally; on the empty
list that is the list head inside struct video_device, so link->source
and everything derived from it is whatever memory follows. On Ubuntu's
6.19.8-surface build that is a pointer into kernel text, and
v4l2_ctrl_g_ctrl() oopses during isys probe:

  Oops: general protection fault, probably for non-canonical address 0x90909090909090c4
  RIP: v4l2_ctrl_g_ctrl+0x1b/0x60 [videodev]
   csi2_try_fmt+0x35/0x60 [intel_ipu4p_isys]
   ipu_isys_csi2_init+0x3ff/0x5d0 [intel_ipu4p_isys]
   isys_probe+0x572/0xdd0 [intel_ipu4p_isys]

Check for an unlinked node and fall back to the store_csi2_header
control's default.

---
--- a/ipu-isys-csi2.c
+++ b/ipu-isys-csi2.c
@@ -675,12 +675,23 @@
 csi2_try_fmt(struct ipu_isys_video *av,
 	     struct v4l2_pix_format_mplane *mpix)
 {
-	struct media_link *link = list_first_entry(&av->vdev.entity.links,
-						   struct media_link, list);
-	struct v4l2_subdev *sd =
-	    media_entity_to_v4l2_subdev(link->source->entity);
+	struct media_link *link;
+	struct v4l2_subdev *sd;
 	struct ipu_isys_csi2 *csi2;
 
+	/*
+	 * Debug capture taps are left unlinked (debug_capture_links=0) but
+	 * ipu_isys_video_init() still runs try_fmt on them. Taking the first
+	 * entry of the empty links list yields the list head itself, and
+	 * link->source then reads whatever follows it in the video node.
+	 * Use the control's default (store CSI-2 headers) instead.
+	 */
+	if (list_empty(&av->vdev.entity.links))
+		return ipu_isys_video_try_fmt_vid_mplane(av, mpix, 1);
+
+	link = list_first_entry(&av->vdev.entity.links, struct media_link,
+				list);
+	sd = media_entity_to_v4l2_subdev(link->source->entity);
 	if (!sd)
 		return NULL;
 
